<div class="wrap">
  <h1 class="page-title">Projects</h1>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-block-start:1.25rem">
    Tools I wanted for my own work, then kept going with. Some are finished, some
    are not, and I am reasonably honest about which is which.
  </p>

  <ul class="projects" style="margin-block-start:3rem">
    <li class="project">
      <h3 class="project__name"><a href="https://abexis.app">ABexis</a></h3>
      <p class="project__what">
        A/B testing rendered at the edge rather than in the browser. Client-side
        testing tools inject an anti-flicker snippet that blocks rendering; that
        is a mechanism problem, not a vendor problem, so the fix has to be
        architectural. Running real tests before it opens up properly.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="project">
      <h3 class="project__name"><a href="https://directorsdraw.uk">Directors Draw</a></h3>
      <p class="project__what">
        What a UK company director actually takes home once salary, dividends,
        corporation tax and pension contributions have all argued with each
        other. Built because I got tired of doing it in a spreadsheet.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="project">
      <h3 class="project__name"><a href="https://abtests.co.uk">abtests.co.uk</a></h3>
      <p class="project__what">
        Writing about conversion rate optimisation where you can toggle between
        the variants on the page rather than look at screenshots of them.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="project">
      <h3 class="project__name">Staffalytic</h3>
      <p class="project__what">
        Cookieless, first-party analytics aimed specifically at student and rental
        housing operators — the metrics that matter there are not the ones a
        general analytics tool puts in front of you. In progress.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="project">
      <h3 class="project__name"><a href="https://scl.im">scl.im</a></h3>
      <p class="project__what">
        A link shortener on Cloudflare Workers. Unglamorous, and I use it every day.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
